  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "VRChat has a profanity filter for strings in world names, user bios, etc. It would be nice if the SDK had a method such as `public static string FilterProfanity(string input)` which would run the same rules on an arbitrary string.\n\nUse-Case: When allowing users to input strings, we would have to implement our own filter if we want our world to be safer for all audiences. If VRChat can expose their own filter, then we can ensure all user-submitted strings can adhere to VRChat's standards.\n\nHere are examples I've seen or thought of where users could enter strings:\n\n* Answer or prompt in a game world\n\n* Title/description for artwork or other UGC\n\n* Custom badge for roleplay purposes\n\n* Name for a custom pet",
